00:02:13.327 --> 00:02:18.527
An investor who wants income rather than a pure commodity spike opens a brokerage screener,

00:02:18.847 --> 00:02:25.487
filters TSX dividend aristocrats for yields above 4% and payout ratios below 70%.

00:02:25.487 --> 00:02:29.587
Then sizes the name inside a tax-free savings account, or TFSA.

00:02:30.107 --> 00:02:35.567
The rule is simple, at least 25 straight years of dividend increases, and a payout ratio

00:02:35.567 --> 00:02:37.567
that free cash flow can actually cover.

00:02:38.187 --> 00:02:45.107
Fool.ca puts Enbridge through that filter with 31 consecutive years of raises and a 5.8% yield

00:02:45.107 --> 00:02:47.107
at $67.24.

00:02:47.747 --> 00:02:54.287
$8,000 in that stock can throw off $462 of dividends in a year, which is the cash flow

00:02:54.287 --> 00:02:57.287
picture the screen is built to find, not a price forecast.

00:02:58.047 --> 00:03:03.387
In the second quarter, the company reaffirmed 2026 guidance and pointed to a $41 billion

00:03:03.387 --> 00:03:08.967
dollar backlog of secured projects, and Chief Executive Officer Greg Ebel said the industry

00:03:08.967 --> 00:03:14.807
has re-entered a growth phase, somewhat reminiscent of the 2012-2015 stretch.

00:03:15.547 --> 00:03:21.347
Endbridge ended the second quarter with a debt-to-ebit-daw ratio of 5.1 times, that is earnings

00:03:21.347 --> 00:03:27.027
before interest, taxes, depreciation, and amortization, which management tied to a weaker

00:03:27.027 --> 00:03:32.427
Canadian dollar, while the adjusted figure sits inside its 4.5 to 5 times target.

00:03:32.427 --> 00:03:37.487
Think of the 25-year raise streak like a tenant who has increased the rent they pay you

00:03:37.487 --> 00:03:39.587
every January for 25 winters.

00:03:40.087 --> 00:03:44.307
You still open the books to confirm they can afford next year's bump, and that check

00:03:44.307 --> 00:03:45.347
is the payout ratio.

00:03:45.967 --> 00:03:50.687
The same screen still works when rate hike years like 2022 knock growth names around,

00:03:51.187 --> 00:03:52.587
because the check keeps clearing.

00:03:53.167 --> 00:03:57.567
It lags when the tape pays only for pure growth and coverage ratios start to compress.

00:03:57.567 --> 00:04:05.787
T.C. energy sits near $87 after a steep pullback, yields about 4% and has raised for 26 consecutive

00:04:05.787 --> 00:04:11.767
years with plans to double capacity on coastal gas link, the pipe that feeds Canadian gas into

00:04:11.767 --> 00:04:16.267
the new liquefied natural gas or LNG, Canada export facility.

00:04:16.767 --> 00:04:25.187
That is dividend income screening, history plus coverage, then a TFSA allocation, not

00:04:25.187 --> 00:04:30.547
Novice Energy, ticker CVE, is the simulated weekly hold, and this is a simulated trade

00:04:30.547 --> 00:04:32.627
for learning purposes with no real money.

00:04:33.147 --> 00:04:37.767
It demonstrates today's dividend income screen inside a sector that already has relative

00:04:37.767 --> 00:04:41.087
strength, rather than grabbing the fattest yield on the board.

00:04:41.687 --> 00:04:47.227
The catalyst is rising crude and natural gas supporting sector leadership, plus a 26-year

00:04:47.227 --> 00:04:52.227
payout growth streak and base dividend increases at a double-digit annual rate for six straight

00:04:52.227 --> 00:04:57.187
years, with management anticipating annual dividend growth above 10%.

00:04:57.187 --> 00:05:02.167
Shares are trading above the 50-day moving average on the daily chart, with volume confirmation

00:05:02.167 --> 00:05:03.347
on recent sessions.

00:05:03.867 --> 00:05:08.907
There is no earnings release inside the five-session window, so that second factor is missing on

00:05:08.907 --> 00:05:09.267
purpose.

00:05:09.907 --> 00:05:15.107
You have a long payout record, commodity prices still elevated, and no print inside the

00:05:15.107 --> 00:05:15.347
hold.

00:05:15.907 --> 00:05:19.427
Do you sit on your hands until the call, or do you take the sector's strength with

00:05:19.427 --> 00:05:20.107
a written stop?

00:05:20.107 --> 00:05:26.707
Here is how I grade it, confidence is medium, two aligned factors, price catalyst plus payout

00:05:26.707 --> 00:05:32.067
history, with sector rotation and support, and the missing earnings catalyst is the uncertainty

00:05:32.067 --> 00:05:37.607
that keeps it off high. Invalidation is named before entry. If the next quarterly dividend

00:05:37.607 --> 00:05:44.007
coverage ratio falls below 1.1 times on the November call, the sustainability thesis is broken.

00:05:44.007 --> 00:05:50.787
The stop loss is 8% below entry, which caps the loss at $80 on the $1,000 position.

00:05:51.347 --> 00:05:57.587
The target is plus 2% to plus 5% over 5 sessions, and the hold exits at the 5th sessions

00:05:57.587 --> 00:06:02.127
close or at that stop, whichever comes first with no discretionary exits.

00:06:02.787 --> 00:06:07.067
It enters at the next sessions open under the published rules and is scored against the

00:06:07.067 --> 00:06:09.807
Nasdaq composite over those same 5 sessions.

00:06:09.807 --> 00:06:15.667
The last dividend income film on the book, Enbridge, carried the same medium grade on a mixed

00:06:15.667 --> 00:06:16.047
setup.

00:06:16.487 --> 00:06:22.887
That is why Sinova stays medium, stays at $1,000, and why this sim writes the 8% stop before

00:06:22.887 --> 00:06:27.927
the open, because the prior sim had no stop the tracker could read, and had to live on

00:06:27.927 --> 00:06:29.167
the horizon exit alone.

00:06:29.747 --> 00:06:34.567
The rules-based book is still behind the NASDAQ on matched windows, so I am not stretching

00:06:34.567 --> 00:06:36.187
size to chase the energy tape.

00:06:36.187 --> 00:06:41.687
The MEG Energy Deal and the Christina Lake North Assets, plus further debt reduction,

00:06:42.007 --> 00:06:45.787
sit behind the cash flow story, not inside this five-session bet.

00:06:46.487 --> 00:06:50.587
Friday's close finished the end bridge weekly hold we simulated from the Monday open.

00:06:51.127 --> 00:07:00.407
We simulated buying ENB at $67.41 on that Monday open and exited at $67.27 on Friday's

00:07:00.407 --> 00:07:07.667
clothes, five sessions, a loss of 0.21%, or $2.08 on the $1,000 position.

00:07:08.287 --> 00:07:15.627
The NASDAQ composite lost 1.53% over the same window, so the trade produced plus 1.32%

00:07:15.627 --> 00:07:18.887
of alpha, even though the dollar result was a scratch lower.

00:07:19.587 --> 00:07:25.387
Stated confidence was medium, the stated invalidation was a coverage ratio under 1.1 times

00:07:25.387 --> 00:07:27.867
on the November call, and it never mattered.

00:07:27.867 --> 00:07:31.727
The sim could not read a stop, so the horizon was the only exit.

00:07:32.347 --> 00:07:36.907
The medium grade fit a mixed setup, and the horizon exit kept the small relative gain,

00:07:37.307 --> 00:07:38.307
while the index fell.

00:07:38.847 --> 00:07:43.207
I would still rather have a written stop on the next one, which is why today's Sennelvis

00:07:43.207 --> 00:07:45.007
ticket names 8% up front.

